and healing them was possible.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:27.360
So, after perhaps a similar&nbsp;
surgery, when this new AI recovered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:32.580
it was also able to do three amazing&nbsp;
things that I really didn’t expect.

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:41.640
One, it can juggle the ball with its chest. Two,&nbsp;
oh yes, this. I love this because this showcases&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:48.300
the advantages of a physics-based system for the&nbsp;
ball movement. It can stop the ball with its foot.

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:55.740
Or, three, it can also kick the ball up&nbsp;
to varying heights. And to think that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.740 --> 00:06:00.780
can do all this from just a soup&nbsp;
of motion capture data. That is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:07.560
recorded movement data from real humans.&nbsp;
That is incredible. And remember, it had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:14.940
never seen these objects before. Wow. I cannot&nbsp;
wait to try the video games of the future where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:20.820
